Feature: Patient Account Table Creation and Data Transformation

  The system must create the target table purgo_playground.patient_account in Unity Catalog purgo_databricks, 
  transforming and loading data from purgo_playground.pa_account according to the mapping specification.
  The process must enforce all schema, transformation, validation, and error handling rules as described.

  Background:
    Given the source table purgo_playground.pa_account exists in Unity Catalog purgo_databricks
    And the mapping specification from source_target_mapping_specification (1).xlsx is available
    And the target table purgo_playground.patient_account does not exist or will be dropped if it does

  # Happy Path: Table Creation and Data Load

  Scenario: Drop and Create patient_account table with correct schema
    Given the target table purgo_playground.patient_account may already exist
    When the SQL process is executed to drop the table if it exists
    Then the table purgo_playground.patient_account is dropped
    When the SQL process is executed to create the table with the following columns and datatypes:
      | Column Name                    | Datatype  | Nullable | Length | Constraint/Logic                                                                 |
      | patient_foundation_shipment    | string    | YES      | 255    | Straight move from source                                                        |
      | prescriber_id                  | string    | YES      | 18     | If "Dr." not in prefix, prepend "DR." (case-insensitive) to prescriber_name_c    |
      | prescriber_key                 | string    | YES      |        | If "Dr." not in prefix, prepend "DR." (case-insensitive) to prescriber_name_c_address |
      | patient_sf_id                  | string    | YES      | 18     | Straight move from source (patinet_c)                                            |
      | service_request_type           | string    | YES      | ce     | Straight move from source (recordtypeid)                                         |
      | case_sf_id                     | string    | YES      | 18     | Straight move from source (id)                                                   |
      | account_id                     | string    | YES      | 18     | Straight move from source (accountid)                                            |
      | hash_key                       | string    | YES      |        | Concatenation: patinet_c#recordtypeid#id#accountid                               |
      | last_modified_date             | timestamp | YES      |        | Set to current timestamp at ETL execution                                        |
    Then the table purgo_playground.patient_account is created with the above schema

  Scenario: Load valid patient account records from pa_account
    Given the table purgo_playground.patient_account is created
    And the source table purgo_playground.pa_account contains records
    When the ETL process runs to load data
    Then only records where patinet_c contains "PAT" (case-insensitive, anywhere in string) are loaded
    And for each loaded record:
      | Source Column                | Target Column                | Transformation Logic                                                                 |
      | patient_foundation_shipment  | patient_foundation_shipment  | Straight move                                                                        |
      | prescriber_name_c            | prescriber_id                | If not starts with "Dr." (case-insensitive), prepend "DR." and a space               |
      | prescriber_name_c_address    | prescriber_key               | If not starts with "Dr." (case-insensitive), prepend "DR." and a space               |
      | patinet_c                    | patient_sf_id                | Straight move                                                                        |
      | recordtypeid                 | service_request_type         | Straight move                                                                        |
      | id                           | case_sf_id                   | Straight move                                                                        |
      | accountid                    | account_id                   | Straight move                                                                        |
      | patinet_c, recordtypeid, id, accountid | hash_key         | Concatenate with "#" separator: patinet_c#recordtypeid#id#accountid                  |
      | (none)                       | last_modified_date           | Set to current timestamp at ETL execution                                            |

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven transformation for prescriber_id and prescriber_key
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c="<prescriber_name_c>" and prescriber_name_c_address="<prescriber_name_c_address>"
    When the ETL transformation is applied
    Then prescriber_id is "<expected_prescriber_id>"
    And prescriber_key is "<expected_prescriber_key>"

    Examples:
      | prescriber_name_c      | prescriber_name_c_address | expected_prescriber_id | expected_prescriber_key |
      | "Dr. John Smith"      | "Dr. Alice Brown"         | "Dr. John Smith"      | "Dr. Alice Brown"      |
      | "John Smith"          | "Alice Brown"             | "DR. John Smith"      | "DR. Alice Brown"      |
      | "DR. John Smith"      | "DR. Alice Brown"         | "DR. John Smith"      | "DR. Alice Brown"      |
      | "dr. John Smith"      | "dr. Alice Brown"         | "dr. John Smith"      | "dr. Alice Brown"      |
      | "john smith"          | "alice brown"             | "DR. john smith"      | "DR. alice brown"      |

  Scenario Outline: Filtering records by patinet_c containing "PAT"
    Given a source record with patinet_c="<patinet_c>"
    When the ETL filter is applied
    Then the record is <load_status> into patient_account

    Examples:
      | patinet_c         | load_status   |
      | "PAT123456"       | loaded        |
      | "pat987654"       | loaded        |
      | "123PAT456"       | loaded        |
      | "123456"          | skipped       |
      | "XYZPAT"          | loaded        |
      | "xyzpat"          | loaded        |
      | "XYZ"             | skipped       |

  # Error Scenarios

  Scenario Outline: Handling missing or invalid source data
    Given a source record with <column> value <value>
    When the ETL process runs
    Then the target column <target_column> is set to <expected_result>

    Examples:
      | column                  | value         | target_column            | expected_result |
      | patient_foundation_shipment | NULL      | patient_foundation_shipment | NULL           |
      | prescriber_name_c           | NULL      | prescriber_id               | NULL           |
      | prescriber_name_c_address   | NULL      | prescriber_key              | NULL           |
      | patinet_c                   | NULL      | patient_sf_id               | NULL           |
      | recordtypeid                | NULL      | service_request_type        | NULL           |
      | id                          | NULL      | case_sf_id                  | NULL           |
      | accountid                   | NULL      | account_id                  | NULL           |

  Scenario: Handling duplicate hash_key values
    Given multiple source records produce the same hash_key value
    When the ETL process runs
    Then all records are loaded into patient_account (no deduplication)
    And no error is raised

  Scenario: Handling invalid data formats
    Given a source record with accountid longer than 18 characters
    When the ETL process runs
    Then the account_id in patient_account is truncated to 18 characters

  Scenario: Handling SQL environment and dialect
    Given the SQL is executed in Unity Catalog purgo_databricks on Databricks SQL
    When the SQL uses data types and functions
    Then only Databricks SQL compatible types and functions are used

  # Validation Rules

  Scenario: Validate hash_key format
    Given a loaded record in patient_account
    When the hash_key is generated
    Then it must be in the format "<patinet_c>#<recordtypeid>#<id>#<accountid>"

  Scenario: Validate last_modified_date
    Given a loaded record in patient_account
    When the ETL process runs
    Then last_modified_date is set to the current timestamp of ETL execution

  # Error Message Scenarios

  Scenario Outline: Error message for invalid filter
    Given a source record with patinet_c="<patinet_c>"
    When the ETL filter is applied and the record does not contain "PAT"
    Then the record is skipped
    And an error message "Record skipped: patinet_c does not contain 'PAT'" is logged

    Examples:
      | patinet_c   |
      | "123456"    |
      | "XYZ"       |

  Scenario Outline: Error message for invalid data length
    Given a source record with <column> value exceeding allowed length
    When the ETL process runs
    Then the value is truncated
    And an error message "Value for <column> truncated to <length> characters" is logged

    Examples:
      | column      | length |
      | accountid   | 18     |
      | patinet_c   | 18     |
      | prescriber_id | 18   |

  # Acceptance Criteria

  Scenario: Acceptance criteria for patient_account table creation and load
    Given the ETL process completes
    Then the table purgo_playground.patient_account exists with the correct schema
    And all records loaded meet the transformation, filtering, and validation rules
    And error scenarios are handled and logged as specified
    And the process is compatible with Databricks SQL in Unity Catalog purgo_databricks

